use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Dismissal import Dismissal
from ../../../behaviors/Positioning import Positioning
from ../../../behaviors/Presence import Presence

export ui-component Popover:
    description:
        A popover is a panel that pops up above the page, attached to the thing
        that opened it, such as a button. The rest of the page stays usable
        while it's open.

    behaviors:
        - @{Positioning}
        - @{Dismissal}
        - @{Presence}

    opening:
        The component using the popover decides what opens it, usually
        pressing the thing it's attached to. That thing tells assistive tools
        whether the popover is open. Pressing it again closes the popover.

    triggers:
        Several things can share one popover, such as an info button on each
        row of a table. The popover attaches to whichever one opened it. If the
        user opens it from another while it's open, it moves there without
        closing. Only that one is shown as open, and focus goes back to it
        when the popover closes.

    focus:
        The component decides whether focus moves into the popover when it
        opens. A popover holding a small form moves focus into it, to the first
        thing that can take focus unless the component names something else. A
        Combobox's list leaves focus in the text box.

    tabOrder:
        Tabbing moves through the popover as if it sat straight after the thing
        that opened it, wherever it is actually drawn. Tabbing past its last
        item moves on to whatever follows the opener, and the popover closes
        because focus has left it.

    closing:
        It closes the ways Dismissal describes: Escape, clicking outside, or
        focus moving away. Focus then goes back to whatever opened it. It may
        also have its own close button.

    content:
        Anything the component puts in it. If it has a title or a short
        description, they are linked to it so assistive tools read them out
        when the user moves into it.

    arrow:
        It may show a small arrow pointing at the thing it's attached to. The
        arrow follows where the popover actually ended up, so if Positioning
        moves it above instead of below, the arrow points down instead of up.

    nonGoals:
        - It doesn't block the rest of the page. A panel that does is a Dialog
        - It doesn't open on hover. A hint that appears on hover is a Tooltip
